# __APP_NAME__

A branded [StoryLark](https://github.com/StoryLark/storylark) site, created with
`npm create storylark`. The engine comes from npm (`storylark-core` +
`storylark-worker` + `storylark-pipeline`, pinned exactly); this folder owns only the brand theme
(`brands/__BRAND_ID__/`), content, and deployment config.

## Deploy

```
npm run setup
```

Runs the setup wizard — pick your platform (Cloudflare or Azure), answer a
few questions, verify the result, then confirm deployment. See
`platforms/cloudflare/README.md` or `platforms/azure/README.md` for the full
manual steps if you'd rather not use the wizard.

Check the installation without changing anything:

```
npm run doctor
npm run doctor -- --json
```

## Brand your site

Edit `brands/__BRAND_ID__/brand.json` and `theme.css` — see
[build-your-own-theme.md](https://github.com/StoryLark/storylark/blob/main/docs/build-your-own-theme.md)
in the engine repo, or start from a theme in the
[gallery](https://gallery.storylark.dev).

## Publish content

```
npm run publish -- --source content
```

StoryLark supports both standalone `type: story` files and multi-chapter books
with one `type: book` declaration plus ordered `type: chapter` files. See
[authoring-stories.md](https://github.com/StoryLark/storylark/blob/main/docs/authoring-stories.md).

## Day to day

```
npm run dev
npm run build
npm run typecheck
```
